{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And He added in the explanation of the utterance <b>“You shall not covet,”</b> that He placed the wife first, because the inclination of man's heart is evil from his youth regarding a woman more than anything. And He explained that desire too falls within the general category of coveting, for if one desires to take by force from one's fellow anything that is his, and cannot do so because his fellow is stronger than he, or because there is fear of the ruling authority in his place — he nonetheless transgresses this negative prohibition. And He added here <b>“his field,”</b> to expound what they said in the Mekhilta (Yitro, ch. 8): If the specific term is spelled out regarding movable property that has no lien upon it, then I have only movable property that has no lien upon it. But when He says in the Mishneh Torah “his field,” perforce the specific term spelled out concerns something that is acquired and transferred by acquisition, hence all things that are acquired and transferred by acquisition are included."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The Hebrew מַכְנֶה is rendered literally as 'transferred by acquisition'; it may carry a technical halakhic nuance of formal transfer."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:50.666640526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}